| Architecture governance | **Very strong, but status can drift** |
| Biggest risk | **Documentation/specification outrunning executable architecture** |

### My central conclusion

I would **not replace the Wheel architecture**.

I would evolve it into a more rigorously enforced architecture:

> **Immutable worker runtime + explicit request scope + inward dependency contracts + domain-owned state + infrastructure adapters + executable architecture rules.**

That preserves the project's central architectural idea while removing the biggest sources of future coupling.

