## Area 1 — Architecture & Dependency Model

### Six-ring Wheel architecture
✅ **Confirmed.** README §"Architecture" shows the six rings verbatim (Outer Rim → Outer Spokes → Inner Rim → Inner Spokes → Hub → Core), and the inner-most ring is Core. INDEX.md declares itself "the single source of truth" for tier mapping.

### "Dependencies point inward"
✅ **Confirmed.** Sampled: `App\Controller\HelloController` imports `SovereignStack\Core\Http\...`. The Core packages (`packages/core/*/src/`) have zero `use App\…` or `use SovereignStack\Hub\…` imports. ADR-004 ("Tier enforcement DAG") codifies this.

### "Architecture is more mature than the application layer"
✅ **Confirmed, and stronger than the architect stated.** Current package distribution:

| Tier | Implemented packages | Blueprints |
|---|---|---|
| Core | **11** (config, container, crypto, dbal, error-handler, event-dispatcher, http-message, kernel, logger, middleware, router) | 20 |
| Hub | **1** (config only — HUB-30) | 31 |
| Spoke/Internal | **1** (codex — ISPOKE-09 stub) | 15–27 |
| Spoke/External | **1** (canvas — ESPOKE-01 stub) | 15–18 |
| Bridge | **1** (vanguard — BRIDGE-01) | 1 |
| Deploy | (Anvil trio runs; not a Composer package) | 5 |

Core: 11 of 20 blueprints implemented (55%). Everything else: 4 of 81 (5%). The architect's "asymmetric Wheel" metaphor is exactly right.

### ⚠️ "8 implemented Core packages" — OUTDATED
The architect said 8. Actual count is **11**. The discrepancy is CORE-16 (Encryption, just merged in `d0ab644`), CORE-18 (Kernel), and CORE-19 (DBAL — has `composer.json` and source files at `packages/core/dbal/src/`). The README at line 30 also still claims "8 Core-tier packages" — same staleness vector.

