### "JWT/rate-limiting/audit are pass-through stubs"
✅ **Confirmed verbatim.** `public/index.php` line 24–25:
> "JWT verification, rate limiting, and HUB-06 audit are pass-through stubs. When HUB-02/HUB-04/HUB-06 land, the stubs are replaced — the chain order and public/index.php are unchanged."

### `public/index.php` is doing too much (composition-root critique)
✅ **Confirmed.** 274 lines, directly constructs: Container, ConfigRepository, ErrorHandler + PlainTextRenderer, EventDispatcher + ListenerProvider, Logger, Vanguard + ContractRegistry + WafInspector + DefaultDtoTransformer, ResponseFactory, Kernel + 5 factory closures, anonymous bootstrapper class, 2 Route instances, 2 controller bindings. This is exactly what the architect describes. The "Outer Rim is currently also a composition root" finding is accurate.

### Area 1 net verdict
**Confirmed with two important corrections:** (1) Core package count is 11, not 8. (2) The Kernel ceilings + lifecycle record feature, although nominally merged in PRs #253/#256/#257, is not present in the working tree at HEAD — either it's on an unmerged branch or got squashed out. The architect should be told. The architectural-direction claims (worker/Fiber model, frozen infra, dependency inwardness, README drift) are all solid.

