## Gathering Results

Evaluation MUST focus on architectural invariants rather than raw code volume or coverage percentage.

### Architecture

Target:

```text
Forbidden ring imports = 0
Service locator violations = 0
Undeclared architecture violations = 0
```

---

### Worker safety

Target:

```text
Cross-request state leaks = 0
Cross-Fiber state leaks = 0
Unexpected worker contamination = 0
```

---

### Runtime

Measure:

```text
worker restart rate
worker recycle rate
graceful shutdown success
request failure during recycling
```

---

### Observability

Every sampled production request SHOULD be traceable through:

```text
request_id
trace_id
edge log
application log
runtime events
error response where applicable
```

---

### Error handling

Measure:

```text
uncategorized errors = 0
error logs without error class = 0
unsafe error responses = 0
```

---

### Deployment

Measure:

```text
candidate verification success rate
deployment rollback time
failed candidate traffic switches
health recovery time
```

A deployment MUST NOT be considered successful merely because `/health` returns HTTP 200.

---

### Performance

Record:

```text
P50
P95
P99
5xx rate
request throughput
worker memory behavior
worker recycling behavior
```

Numerical SLO targets SHOULD be selected after representative baseline measurements.

The architecture specification deliberately does not invent latency targets.

---

### Contractor acceptance matrix

| Area | Acceptance condition |
|---|---|
| Architecture | Ring violations fail CI |
| DI | Forbidden service locator fails CI |
| Worker runtime | Concurrent request state remains isolated |
| Kernel | Lifecycle invariants pass |
| Immutability | Frozen structures reject mutation |
| Composition | `public/index.php` remains thin |
| Domain | Domain has no infrastructure coupling |
| Persistence | Repository ports point inward |
| Transactions | Application service owns transaction |
| Events | Runtime/domain/integration semantics remain separate |
| Observability | Request/trace IDs propagate correctly |
| Errors | Five-class taxonomy is enforced |
| Deployment | Candidate passes full-stack verification before activation |
| Blue/green | Failed candidate can be rolled back |
| Health | Liveness/readiness/dependency semantics are distinct |
| Status | Generated architecture status matches repository reality |

---

### Final architectural principle

DGLab should evolve according to the following rule:

> **Do not add architecture merely because the framework can support it. Add architecture when a concrete requirement needs it, and make every important architectural invariant executable.**

The existing runtime should therefore be preserved.

The next major engineering effort is not a rewrite of Core or Anvil. It is the controlled transition from:

```text
documented architecture
```

to:

```text
executable architecture
```

and then from:

```text
runtime foundation
```

to:

```text
well-isolated Hub/domain/application functionality
```

That gives contractors a concrete implementation boundary while protecting the architecture already established in DGLab.

