## §8. RequestContext

### Proposed `final readonly class RequestContext` with `requestId, traceId, ?tenantId, \DateTimeImmutable $startedAt`
💬 **Sound design.** Follows the existing `TenantContext` pattern exactly: immutable value object, constructor-injected, no static accessor. The `readonly class` syntax is PHP 8.4-supported (verified — composer.json requires `^8.4`).

### "If a tenant is established later in request processing, the context SHOULD be replaced with a new immutable instance rather than mutated."
💬 **Critical design discipline.** This is the right pattern — replace, don't mutate. Preserves immutability. The implementation cost is one extra `RequestContext` instantiation per request when tenant is established post-routing (e.g., after JWT authentication).

