### ADR-013 itself has drift — SPEC correctly flags this
✅ **Important sub-finding.** I re-verified ADR-013 text:

> "The **PostgreSQL driver is shipped but disabled** (`enabled: false` in the default `core.database.drivers` config)"

But `packages/core/dbal/src/Driver/` contains only `MysqlDriver.php` and `SqliteDriver.php` — **no PostgreSQL driver file exists**. So ADR-013's own text is wrong about the PostgreSQL driver being "shipped." The SPEC's call to document this as "repository/ADR drift" is exactly right — both ADR-013 itself and the broader README/INDEX have the same drift disease.

### Dev environment confirms MySQL
✅ **Additional verification.** `anvil/dev/Caddyfile.dev` line 32 sets:
```
env DB_DSN="mysql:host=127.0.0.1;port=3306;dbname=dglab_dev"
```

So the dev datastore is also MySQL, not PostgreSQL. Consistent end-to-end.

