## §27. Safe Error Responses

### "Internal exception details MUST remain internal. Production HTTP responses MUST NOT expose: stack traces; source paths; SQL; credentials; connection strings; environment variables; internal service topology; cryptographic material."
💬 **Sound security discipline.** The `display_errors=Off` enforcement in ErrorHandler (line 69) already prevents PHP's default stack-trace leak. The SPEC extends this to all response surfaces.

### "The request ID allows operators to correlate the public response with internal logs without exposing internal diagnostics."
💬 **Critical operational discipline.** This is exactly the right contract: clients get a correlation key, operators get the diagnostics, neither leaks to the other side.

