## §41. Container Service-Locator Rule — `resolve(` refinement properly absorbed

✅ **Part 2 correction properly absorbed.** §41 now narrows the forbidden pattern to:

> "The rule MUST specifically detect container receivers such as:
> `$container->resolve(...)`
> `Container::resolve(...)`
> and equivalent container-specific resolution patterns.
>
> It MUST NOT generically ban:
> `->resolve(...)`
> because legitimate existing methods include:
> - `MiddlewareResolver::resolve()`
> - `ContractRegistry::resolve()`
> - `PerRequestHandler` resolution
> - `Vanguard` resolution"

This is exactly what I recommended in Part 2 verification. The architect correctly:
1. Narrowed the forbidden pattern from blanket `->resolve(` to container-specific receivers
2. Explicitly listed the four legitimate `resolve()` callers in the existing codebase
3. Added the discipline "False positives are covered by regression tests"

I verified all four legitimate callers exist:
- `MiddlewareResolver::resolve()` ✅ (`packages/core/middleware/src/MiddlewareResolver.php`)
- `ContractRegistry::resolve()` ✅ (`packages/bridge/vanguard/src/ContractRegistry.php`)
- `PerRequestHandler` resolution ✅ (calls `$this->resolver->resolve($entry)` in `PerRequestHandler.php`)
- `Vanguard` resolution ✅ (calls `$this->contracts->resolve($route)` in `Vanguard.php`)

All four legitimate callers will pass the narrowed CI rule.

