## §42. Phase 2 — Request Context and Worker Isolation

### "Create an immutable `RequestContext` based on the existing `TenantContext` design."
✅ **Sound — extends existing pattern as recommended.** The 5 fields (`request_id`, `trace_id`, `tenant_id?`, `started_at`, `route_name?`) match what I proposed in Area 10. The explicit instruction to use the existing `TenantContext` design (immutable value object, no static accessor, Fiber-scoped via existing `WeakMap<Fiber, ...>`) is exactly right.

### "Do not introduce static request state."
💬 **Critical discipline.** Verified — `TenantContext` has no static accessor; the SPEC's continuation of this pattern is correct.

