## §46. Phase 5 — Hub Vertical Slice

### "Select one representative business capability and implement it end-to-end"
💬 **Sound YAGNI discipline.** Implementing one capability end-to-end proves the pattern before mass-implementing all 30 Hub blueprints.

### The vertical slice flow: HTTP/API → Application Command → Application Service → Domain Aggregate → Repository Port → Persistence Adapter → Core DBAL → MySQL/InnoDB
💬 **Sound — exactly the ports-and-adapters pattern from §18.** The 9-item deliverable list (domain entity/value object, aggregate boundary, domain invariant, repository port, MySQL adapter, application service, transaction boundary, error mapping, tests) is comprehensive.

### "This slice becomes the template for future Hub capabilities."
💬 **Critical discipline.** One proven vertical slice is worth more than 30 horizontal stubs.

