11. **State machines** — Product: draft → published → archived; Course: one-way (no unarchive); Enrollment: active → cancelled/completed; Progress: not_started → in_progress → completed
12. **Module immutability** — published-course module IDs are immutable (cannot be deleted; can add/update/replace)
13. **Filesystem/DB consistency** — write-then-cleanup; never delete file when commit outcome unknown; reconciliation handles ambiguous state; interval is configuration
14. **Read-side architecture** — CQRS-ish split; query interfaces return DTOs (not aggregates); cross-aggregate read via dedicated query interface; controllers use query interfaces only, aggregate repositories inside write services
15. **Authorization** — self vs on-behalf; product-namespaced roles; Identity owns role facts, products own policy
16. **Event infrastructure** — deferred (M6) until real async requirement; post-commit dispatch for MVP
17. **Composition Principle** — compose downward, abstract upward, expose only the capability contract; new packages are plugs that abstract existing cables; each plug has a specific reason to exist

