### 3. Lap 2 Admission Strategy

Lap 2 follows the canonical Spiral Deepening rule:

```text
Lap 2
 ├── Widen
 │    └── admit next dependency-supported blueprint(s)
 │
 └── Deepen
      └── existing Lap 1 blueprints by +1 depth
```

The per-blueprint floor remains relative to each blueprint's admission lap. A blueprint admitted at depth 2 during Lap 1 therefore targets depth 3 during Lap 2; newly widened blueprints enter at depth 1 and are not expected to jump multiple depth levels in the same cycle. This is the explicit anti-cliff rule in the canonical SDLC. citeturn2view0

#### Deepening candidates

The five Lap 1 work units be([GitHub](https://github.com/DGCodeIdeas/DGLab/blob/main/Architecture/CrossCutting/SDLC-AGRD.md))irical deepening cohort.

The target is:

```text
Lap 1 result             Lap 2 target
──────────────────────────────────────
Filesystem depth 2   →   depth 3
Identity depth 2     →   depth 3
Showcase depth 2     →   depth 3
RequestContext       →   next defined depth
Health                →   next defined depth
```

The exact depth mapping for RequestContext and Health MUST be taken from their current blueprint/status records rather than inferred from package names.

This cohort is also the mechanism for measuring the previously unknown deepening throughput.

