# 10. Make CI reject architectural documentation drift

The PR gate should become:

```text
composer validate
        │
        ▼
unit/integration tests
        │
        ▼
architecture boundary lint
        │
        ▼
architecture fitness
        │
        ▼
generate architecture status
        │
        ▼
documentation fidelity
        │
        ▼
PASS / FAIL
```

If source changes alter architecture state, but the generated documentation isn't updated:

```text
❌ architecture state changed
❌ generated documentation stale
```

The PR cannot merge.

This is substantially better than discovering drift during a later SDLC reconciliation.

---

# 11. Make the generated output reproducible

Do **not** put timestamps into committed generated architecture files unless necessary.

Prefer:

```json
{
  "source_commit": "e74ad1d",
  "schema_version": 1,
  ...
}
```

rather than:

```json
"generated_at": "2026-09-26T14:22:31Z"
```

Otherwise every generation creates meaningless diffs.

If you need timestamps, put them only in CI artifacts.

