# 12. Fix the README only after the machinery exists

This ordering matters.

I would **not** first spend time manually correcting the README.

Instead:

### Phase A — machinery

1. Define authority hierarchy.
2. Build canonical architecture-status command.
3. Derive package inventory from Composer.
4. Derive dependency graph from Composer.
5. Derive implemented/blueprint state.
6. Validate architecture policy.
7. Add FF-04 documentation fidelity.

### Phase B — migration

8. Generate the canonical current status.
9. Rewrite README volatile sections.
10. Replace stale hand-written architecture tables.
11. Mark historical architecture documents explicitly.
12. Link narrative documentation to generated state.

### Phase C — enforcement

13. Add CI gate.
14. Test deliberate documentation drift.
15. Test deliberate dependency drift.
16. Test deliberate tier violation.
17. Test deliberate blueprint/status mismatch.

Only then call the drift correction complete.

